diff --git a/Docs/MoltenVK_Configuration_Parameters.md b/Docs/MoltenVK_Configuration_Parameters.md
index fdb7b9fa..43daff7f 100644
--- a/Docs/MoltenVK_Configuration_Parameters.md
+++ b/Docs/MoltenVK_Configuration_Parameters.md
@@ -658,3 +658,19 @@ In the special case of `VK_SEMAPHORE_TYPE_TIMELINE` semaphores, **MoltenVK** wil
 Makes MoltenVK treat all descriptors as if they had `VK_DESCRIPTOR_BINDING_PARTIALLY_BOUND_BIT` set.
 Versions of MoltenVK with this flag are less forgiving of applications that bind descriptors that point to
 destroyed objects, so this option can be used to temporarily work around any breakage that may have caused.
+
+----------------------------------------
+#### MVK_CONFIG_ADVERTISE_ROBUST_BUFFER_ACCESS_2
+
+##### Type: Boolean
+##### Default: `1`
+
+Advertise the `VkPhysicalDeviceRobustness2FeaturesEXT::robustBufferAccess2` feature
+(on Apple family GPUs only).
+
+Metal does not bounds-check buffer accesses in shaders, and MoltenVK does not inject
+MSL bounds checks, so out-of-bounds behaviour is not strictly guaranteed by MoltenVK
+itself. On Apple family GPUs, out-of-bounds buffer accesses are contained by the GPU
+memory subsystem in practice, and D3D12 translation layers such as vkd3d-proton apply
+their own shader-level bounds behaviour. Disable this setting if strict Vulkan
+robustness guarantees are required.
